Z||000004||frontal lobe||05-13-2001||01:55 AM||||When you check someone's blood pressure, if the cuff size is too small relative to the person's arm, the blood pressure can read falsely high.  So there are different size cuffs, ranging from pediatric (for kids or skinny armed adults) to normal (or adult) to<BR>large to even a thigh cuff (which is actually supposed to be used on a normal human's thigh to check the blood pressure in the leg, but I actually have patients I have to use it on their arms!!!!)<P>So if I'm using the large cuff a lot, I'm dealing with a pretty hefty bunch of people.  This isn't surprising in Wisconsin, as we have the highest obesity rate in the country.<P>So Stimpy, here's chasing down that cheese with a couple of bratwurst and some cheese fries.  And some cheesecake for dessert. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||05-13-2001||07:49 AM||||My daughter used to live in Roscoe,ILL.When I visited her,I noticed that the average person seemed to be a little larger than back here on the east coast.If you really want to see some BIG people stop at any one of the buffets in my area at feeding time.I have seen four people at one table whose combined weight must have exceeded 1200 pounds,and 3 of them were women,the smallest being a man.The number of overweight people at these buffets is way out of proportion to the general population.I can't blame them though,where else can you eat all you want for just $10.99?||||reg||1
Z||000006||WampusCat||05-13-2001||08:12 AM||||I used to work for an air-ambulance co. in south TX mostly along the border.  Some of those ladies we had to strap on a back board and turn sideways to fit into the aircraft door.  I was amazed at the number of +-39 yr. old heart attacks we flew out of there.  I guess a clue would be the lard aisle in the local supermarket.  Not a lard section, but a lard aisle!  Lets see... do I want the 3 gallon lard bucket or the 5 gallon...||||reg||1
Z||000007||frontal lobe||05-14-2001||12:15 PM||||LARD AISLE!!!  THAT is funny.  Whip some lard up with sugar and you got yourself some frosting.<P>Did you ever worry that the plane wouldn't be able to take off????<P>Hey Hugh, when I was in medical school in Rockford, Il. I used to have to go up to a clinic in Rockton all the time (just by Roscoe).  Things are pretty far spread apart her in the midwest so people don't walk anywhere, either, so no automatic exercise just in daily life.  Now that I think about it, the only exercise I get is lifting myself out of that low Fiero seat.  Oh well, at least that's ONE deep knee bend a day!||||reg||1
